  "body": "### Summary\nAs a reader, when I turn on Réglages › Sujets › « Afficher les signatures », I want each message's signature to show under it, as in the legacy app; today the setting is on and no signature shows (operator device feedback, 2026-11-10).\n\n### Facts (dev-swift `fddb6a37`)\n- Setting: `display_sig` (`SettingKey.displaySignatures`, default off as legacy `AppSettingsView.swift:110` @ `87fe0d1c`), toggle `SettingsView.swift:135` (LOT-106, #460).\n- Reader: `TopicHTMLBuilder.swift:123` appends `<div class=\"signature\">` when `showsSignatures` and `message.content.signatureHTML` is non-nil; `TopicReaderModel.swift:174` rebuilds the page when a display setting changes.\n- Engine: `MessageContentNormalizer` splits `span.signature` out (LOT-034); 24 committed captures hold `class=\"signature\"`.\n- Legacy shows them with a CSS class only (`OnlineMessagesTableViewController.m:1608-1613` @ `87fe0d1c`): the page HFR sends already carries the signatures.\n\n### Scope\n1. Find where the signature is lost, on the real entry point: capture → `TopicPageParser`/normalizer → `ReaderSettings` snapshot → `TopicHTMLBuilder` → `reader.css` (`.signature > br:first-child, .content span.signature { display: none; }` at line 134) → the rebuild on a setting change, and the offline-saved pages.\n2. Fix it; the signature keeps the reader's security (no script, images through the image policy).\n\n### Acceptance criteria\n- A test on a committed capture with signatures: setting on → every signed message renders its `div.signature`; setting off → none. Shown to fail without the fix.\n- A test that toggling the setting while a topic is open shows or hides the signatures without a reload.\n- Mac check on device.\n\nM4 (device feedback). Origin: parity (legacy shows them).\n\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code)_",
